<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Diarra</h1><p class="st-meta">1076 CE – 1754 CE (approx.) · capital Diara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Soninke kingdom of the Sahel north of the Senegal and Niger headwaters that outlived the Ghana Empire by nearly seven centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Diarra, or Diara, arose in the Kingaga region around present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nioro-du-sahel">Nioro du Sahel</a> as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a> fragmented. Tradition dates it to 1076, the year associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire's</a> attack on Ghana. Its first ruling house was the Niakhate clan, later replaced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diawara">Diawara</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Diarra's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soninke">Soninke</a> rulers governed a mixed population of farmers and herders and profited from the trade between the desert and the savanna. The kingdom was usually a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of a larger power, first of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> and then of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a>, while keeping its own dynasties.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 18th century Diarra was overrun by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bambara-people">Bambara</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaarta">Kaarta</a>, who took its lands in 1754, according to the register's dating. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diawara">Diawara</a> remain a recognised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soninke">Soninke</a> clan in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1076 CE – 1754 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.11%;width:13.49%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1076 CE – 1754 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Diara</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam and Soninke traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Soninke</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mali">Mali</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Diara, Kingdom of Diara, Diawara kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1415&amp;focus=kingdom-of-diarra" aria-label="Kingdom of Diarra on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4425 1608 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Diarra lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4745 1864L4769 1989M4745 1864L4999 1829M4745 1864L4782 1851"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4769 1989h0M4999 1829h0M4782 1851h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4745 1864h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4745 1864h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1415&amp;focus=kingdom-of-diarra">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
